  "name": null,
  "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X$ has a student's $t$-distribution ${T}_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom. Given that the random variable $X∼{T}_{12},$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\ge x)=0.005.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $11$ | $\\,1.363\\,$ | $\\,1.796\\,$ | $\\,2.201\\,$ | $\\,2.718\\,$ | $\\,3.106\\,$ |\n| $12$ | $\\,1.356\\,$ | $\\,1.782\\,$ | $\\,2.179\\,$ | $\\,2.681\\,$ | $\\,3.055\\,$ |\n| $13$ | $\\,1.350\\,$ | $\\,1.771\\,$ | $\\,2.160\\,$ | $\\,2.650\\,$ | $\\,3.012\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
